# Tailwind CSS Rules

## Utility Classes
- Use utility classes over custom CSS
- Implement responsive design with mobile-first approach
- Use CSS variables for dynamic colors
- Add dynamic classes to `safelist` in `tailwind.config.ts`
- Use `@apply` directive sparingly

## Responsive Design
```typescript
// Good: Mobile-first responsive design
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
  {pokemonList.map(pokemon => (
    <PokemonCard key={pokemon.id} pokemon={pokemon} />
  ))}
</div>
```

## Dynamic Classes
```typescript
// Good: Use safelist for dynamic classes
const typeColor = `hover:border-${pokemon.types[0].type.name}`;
const typeShadow = `hover:shadow-${pokemon.types[0].type.name}`;

// Add to tailwind.config.ts safelist
safelist: [
  'hover:border-fire',
  'hover:shadow-fire',
  'hover:border-water',
  'hover:shadow-water',
  // ... all type combinations
]
```

## Dark Mode
```typescript
// Good: Dark mode implementation
<div className="bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
  <h1 className="text-2xl font-bold">Pokemon List</h1>
</div>
```

## CSS Variables
```css
/* globals.css */
:root {
  --type-fire: #ff6b6b;
  --type-water: #4ecdc4;
  --type-grass: #45b7d1;
}

.dark {
  --type-fire: #ff8a8a;
  --type-water: #6eddd6;
  --type-grass: #67c3f3;
}
```

## Component Styling
```typescript
// Good: Component with Tailwind classes
export const PokemonCard = ({ pokemon }: { pokemon: Pokemon }) => {
  const type = pokemon.types[0].type.name;
  
  return (
    <div 
      className={`
        bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 
        rounded-lg shadow-md hover:shadow-lg 
        transition-all duration-300 
        hover:scale-105 cursor-pointer
        border-2 border-transparent
        hover:border-${type}
      `}
      style={{
        '--type-color': `var(--type-${type})`,
        borderColor: `var(--type-${type})`,
        boxShadow: `0 0 20px var(--type-${type})`
      }}
    >
      {/* Card content */}
    </div>
  );
};
```

## Avoid
- Don't use inline styles when Tailwind classes work
- Don't create custom CSS for common patterns
- Don't forget to add dynamic classes to safelist
- Don't ignore responsive design principles